description:
The University of Bristol is appointing the services of a suitably qualified transport consultant with an in-depth understanding of the local context to develop site-specific travel plans for two of its campuses:

- Temple Quarter Enterprise Campus, Bristol, BS2 0PX; and
- Langford Campus, North Somerset, BS40 5DU.

The purpose of these campus travel plans is to operationalise the university&#039;s Travel and Transport Delivery Plan at the campus level for TQEC and Langford. As such, the scope of the travel plans should include all types of travel and transport generated by each campus i.e:

- day-to-day commuting by staff, students and partners;
- business and academic travel, including inter-campus trips;
- student termly travel;
- visitor travel; and
- operational transport, including university and contractor fleets, deliveries and collections
